# Model Update Context

This file provides instructions and automation procedures for updating the VS Code `chatLanguageModels.json` configuration file with the latest models from local and networked LM Studio endpoints across **Windows**, **macOS**, and **Linux**.

---

## 1. Target File Paths & Profile Discovery

VS Code stores custom chat model definitions either in the **Default Profile** directory or in a **Custom Profile** directory.

### Path by Operating System

| OS | Default Profile Path | Custom Profile Path |
|----|----------------------|---------------------|
| **Windows** | `%APPDATA%\Code\User\chatLanguageModels.json` | `%APPDATA%\Code\User\profiles\<profile-id>\chatLanguageModels.json` |
| **macOS** | `~/Library/Application Support/Code/User/chatLanguageModels.json` | `~/Library/Application Support/Code/User/profiles/<profile-id>/chatLanguageModels.json` |
| **Linux** | `~/.config/Code/User/chatLanguageModels.json` | `~/.config/Code/User/profiles/<profile-id>/chatLanguageModels.json` |

> [!NOTE]
> If you switch profiles frequently in VS Code, update **both** the active profile (`profiles/<profile-id>/chatLanguageModels.json`) and the base user configuration (`Code/User/chatLanguageModels.json`).

### Active Profile Auto-Detection

To automatically detect the active (most recently modified) profile directory:

**Windows (PowerShell):**
```powershell
# Detect most recently active profile, or fallback to default
$profilesBase = "$env:APPDATA\Code\User\profiles"
$activeProfileDir = Get-ChildItem "$profilesBase\*\globalStorage" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |
    Sort-Object LastWriteTime -Descending | Select-Object -First 1 | ForEach-Object { $_.Parent }

if ($activeProfileDir) {
    $targetPath = Join-Path $activeProfileDir.FullName "chatLanguageModels.json"
} else {
    $targetPath = "$env:APPDATA\Code\User\chatLanguageModels.json"
}
Write-Host "Target configuration path: $targetPath"
```

**macOS / Linux (Bash):**
```bash
PROFILES_BASE="$HOME/.config/Code/User/profiles"
# On macOS: PROFILES_BASE="$HOME/Library/Application Support/Code/User/profiles"

LATEST_PROFILE=$(ls -td "$PROFILES_BASE"/*/globalStorage 2>/dev/null | head -n 1 | xargs dirname)
if [ -n "$LATEST_PROFILE" ]; then
    TARGET_PATH="$LATEST_PROFILE/chatLanguageModels.json"
else
    TARGET_PATH="$HOME/.config/Code/User/chatLanguageModels.json"
fi
echo "Target configuration path: $TARGET_PATH"
```

---

## 2. Categories and Endpoints

The configuration supports cluster categories based on available nodes:

| Category | Endpoint URL | Description |
|----------|-------------|-------------|
| **Local** | `http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1` | Models hosted on the current machine (loopback) |
| **amd-halo** | `http://amd-halo:1234/v1` | Models hosted on AMD Halo device (hostname) |
| **ripper** | `http://ripper:1234/v1` | Models hosted on ripper device (hostname) |
| **geforce** | `http://geforce:1234/v1` | Models hosted on NVIDIA GeForce GPU (hostname) |
| **LM-Link** | `http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1` | All cluster models served via loopback endpoint |
| **Remote** | `http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1` | Remote cluster models routed via loopback |

---

## 3. Host Context ("Local" vs Peer Devices)

When running on different machines:
- **"Local"** always refers to whichever physical device is executing the script/process (`http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1`).
- To inspect which machine is local vs remote, run:
  ```bash
  lms link status
  ```
  The output lists `This device: <name>` (Local) and connected peer devices (e.g. `amd-halo`, `ripper`, `GeForce`, `DTE-macOS-*`).
- If executing directly on `amd-halo`, `Local` becomes `amd-halo`, and workstation devices become remote.

---

## 4. URL Conventions

- Use `127.0.0.1` for the local machine loopback address (**not** `localhost`).
- Use hostnames (`amd-halo`, `ripper`, `geforce`) where DNS/mDNS resolution is available on your local network.
- Peer nodes without a direct LAN hostname (e.g. `DTE-macOS-*` over LM-Link) are accessed through the `LM-Link` and `Remote` categories via loopback (`http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1`).
- **No remote IPs**: All endpoints resolve locally via hostname or loopback — avoid hardcoded external or link-local IPs (`169.254.x.x`).

---

## 5. Model Discovery & Parsing

### Step 1: Wake LM-Link & Run `lms ls`

> [!WARNING]
> **Cold-Start Wakeup Behavior:** If the LM Studio service was asleep (`Waking up LM Studio service...`), the very first `lms ls` call may only return `Local` models while LM-Link peers are still establishing connections. Always run `lms link status` first (and wait 2–3 seconds if waking up) before running `lms ls`.

```bash
# 1. Wake service and verify connected LM-Link peers
lms link status

# 2. List all models with hosting device column
lms ls

# 3. Fetch structured model metadata (displayName, maxContextLength, type)
lms ls --json
```

### Step 2: Handle Multi-Device Models & Plural Variants

- Models may appear under multiple devices simultaneously (e.g. `google/gemma-4-12b-qat` on `Local`, `amd-halo`, `ripper`, and `DTE-macOS-*`).
- Standard text output of `lms ls` may contain singular or plural variant annotations (e.g., `(1 variant)` or `(2 variants)`).
- **Regex pattern for text parsing:**
  ```regex
  ^\s*([^\s(]+)(?:\s+\(\d+\s+variant\w*\))?\s+
  ```
  And capture the device column matching:
  ```regex
  \s+(Local|amd-halo|ripper|GeForce|DTE-macOS-\S+)\b
  ```

### Step 3: Categorize Models

- **`Local`**: Models where `DEVICE == Local`. URL: `http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1`.
- **`amd-halo`**: Models where `DEVICE == amd-halo`. URL: `http://amd-halo:1234/v1`.
- **`ripper`**: Models where `DEVICE == ripper`. URL: `http://ripper:1234/v1`.
- **`geforce`**: Models where `DEVICE == GeForce`. URL: `http://geforce:1234/v1` (keep category even if empty when node is offline).
- **`LM-Link`**: All distinct cluster models returned by `http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1/models`. URL: `http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1`.
- **`Remote`**: All models hosted on any remote peer (`amd-halo`, `ripper`, `GeForce`, `DTE-macOS-*`), routed via `http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1`.

---

## 6. Schema Requirements & Per-Model Context Limits

For each category, define an object with a `models` array in `chatLanguageModels.json`:

```json
{
  "name": "<category-name>",
  "vendor": "customendpoint",
  "apiType": "chat-completions",
  "models": [
    {
      "id": "<model-id>",
      "name": "<display-name>",
      "url": "<endpoint-url>",
      "toolCalling": true,
      "vision": true,
      "maxInputTokens": 65536,
      "maxOutputTokens": 8192
    }
  ]
}
```

### Context Window Allocation (Reasonable Limits $\le$ 100k)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Do not set a blanket 100k context for all models.** Over-allocating context on tiny or embedding models causes out-of-memory errors or exceeds trained context limits. Context sizes must be set to a reasonable limit based on model architecture and parameter count, erroring on the side of higher context by **no more than 100k**:

| Tier | `maxInputTokens` | `maxOutputTokens` | Target Models | Rationale |
|:---|:---:|:---:|:---|:---|
| **94k** | `94208` | `8192` | `google/gemma-4-26b-a4b`<br>`google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-qat`<br>`google/gemma-4-31b`<br>`google/gemma-4-31b-qat`<br>`qwen/qwen3.8-27b`<br>`qwen3.8-27b` | Dedicated long-context prose, RFC/architecture documentation, and Mermaid diagramming specialists (optimal 64k–94k). |
| **65k** | `65536` | `8192` | `deepseek/deepseek-r1-0528-qwen3-8b`<br>`gemma-4-12b-heretic-abliterated`<br>`google/gemma-4-12b`<br>`google/gemma-4-12b-qat`<br>`gpt-oss-120b`<br>`nousresearch/hermes-4-70b`<br>`nvidia/nemotron-3-nano`<br>`nvidia/nemotron-3-super`<br>`nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl`<br>`openai/gpt-oss-20b`<br>`qwen/qwen3-coder-30b`<br>`qwen/qwen3-coder-next`<br>`qwen/qwen3.5-9b`<br>`qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b`<br>`qwen3-coder-30b-a3b-instruct`<br>`qwen3.5-122b-a10b`<br>`qwen3.6-35b-a3b`<br>`qwen3.6-35b-a3b-uncensored-hauhaucs-aggressive`<br>`qwen3.8-27b-uncensored-hauhaucs-aggressive-mtp`<br>`recursivesi/flint`<br>`unsloth/qwen3-coder-next` | Primary backend coding agents, deep reasoning MoEs, and mid-to-large general models. Errs on the high side of their 32k–64k optimal range while avoiding memory bandwidth bottlenecks. |
| **49k** | `49152` | `8192` | `glm-4.7-flash`<br>`google/gemma-4-e4b`<br>`ibm/granite-4-h-tiny`<br>`meta/muse-glimmer`<br>`nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-4b`<br>`nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni`<br>`qwen/qwen3-4b-2507` | Lightweight 4B–7B models, high-speed UI/frontend specialists, and watchdog/helper models. |
| **32k** | `32768` | `4096` | `qwen3-1.7b` | Tiny 1.7B edge/draft model (native max context is 40,960). |
| **2k** | `2048` | `512` | `text-embedding-nomic-embed-text-v1.5` | Local vector embedding model (native max context is 2,048). |

### Dynamic Fallback for New Models

When a newly downloaded model is not yet listed in the static lookup map, scripts automatically fall back to `lms ls --json` metadata:
- **`name`**: Uses `displayName` from `lms ls --json` (or `id` if unavailable).
- **Context limits**:
  - If `type == "embedding"` or `maxContextLength <= 4096`: `maxInputTokens = 2048`, `maxOutputTokens = 512`.
  - If `maxContextLength <= 40960`: `maxInputTokens = 32768`, `maxOutputTokens = 4096`.
  - Otherwise: `maxInputTokens = 65536`, `maxOutputTokens = 8192`.

---

## 7. Safety, Verification & Reload

1. **Backup:** Always create a `.bak` backup copy before writing.
2. **Complete Overwrite:** Write the entire valid JSON structure in one operation. **Never append** to existing arrays to prevent syntax corruption.
3. **Validate Syntax:**
   - PowerShell: `Get-Content $path -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json`
   - Bash: `jq . "$path"`
4. **Verify Endpoints:** Check that no invalid URLs were generated:
   ```powershell
   # Windows PowerShell
   Select-String -Path 'chatLanguageModels.json' -Pattern 'localhost|169\.254\.' | Select-Object LineNumber, Line
   ```
   ```bash
   # macOS / Linux
   grep -n 'localhost\|169\.254\.' chatLanguageModels.json
   ```
   *Expected result: 0 matches.*
5. **Reload VS Code Chat:**
   ```bash
   code --reload-window
   ```
   Or run **Developer: Reload Window** (`Ctrl+Shift+P` / `Cmd+Shift+P`).

---

## 8. Complete Automated PowerShell Script

Save and run this script on Windows to automatically query LM Studio, resolve current and remote model IDs, validate, back up, and update `chatLanguageModels.json` without depending on static hostnames:

```powershell
# update-chat-models.ps1
$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"

# 1. Human-readable name mapping
$nameMap = @{
    "deepseek/deepseek-r1-0528-qwen3-8b"             = "DeepSeek R1 0528 Qwen3 8B"
    "gemma-4-12b-heretic-abliterated"               = "Gemma 4 12B Heretic Abliterated"
    "glm-4.7-flash"                                  = "GLM 4.7 Flash"
    "google/gemma-4-12b"                             = "Gemma 4 12B"
    "google/gemma-4-12b-qat"                         = "Gemma 4 12B QAT"
    "google/gemma-4-26b-a4b"                         = "Gemma 4 26B A4B"
    "google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-qat"                     = "Gemma 4 26B A4B QAT"
    "google/gemma-4-31b"                             = "Gemma 4 31B"
    "google/gemma-4-31b-qat"                         = "Gemma 4 31B QAT"
    "google/gemma-4-e4b"                             = "Gemma 4 E4B"
    "gpt-oss-120b"                                   = "Lemonade GPT OSS 120B (Q4_K_M)"
    "ibm/granite-4-h-tiny"                           = "Granite 4 H Tiny"
    "meta/muse-glimmer"                              = "Meta Muse Glimmer 28B"
    "nousresearch/hermes-4-70b"                      = "Hermes 4 70B"
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-nano"                         = "Nemotron 3 Nano"
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-4b"                      = "Nemotron 3 Nano 4B"
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni"                    = "Nemotron 3 Nano Omni 30B-A3B"
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-super"                        = "Nemotron 3 Super 120B"
    "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl"                   = "Nemotron 3.5 Super VL 120B"
    "openai/gpt-oss-20b"                             = "OpenAI GPT-OSS 20B"
    "qwen/qwen3-4b-2507"                             = "Qwen 3 4B 2507"
    "qwen/qwen3-coder-30b"                           = "Qwen 3 Coder 30B"
    "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"                          = "Qwen 3 Coder Next"
    "qwen/qwen3.5-9b"                                = "Qwen 3.5 9B"
    "qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b"                           = "Qwen 3.6 35B A3B"
    "qwen/qwen3.8-27b"                               = "Qwen 3.8 27B"
    "qwen3-1.7b"                                     = "Qwen 3 1.7B"
    "qwen3-coder-30b-a3b-instruct"                   = "Unsloth Qwen 3 Coder 30B A3B Instruct"
    "qwen3.5-122b-a10b"                              = "Qwen 3.5 122B A10B (Unsloth Q4_K_M)"
    "qwen3.6-35b-a3b"                                = "Qwen 3.6 35B A3B (Unsloth Q8_0)"
    "qwen3.6-35b-a3b-uncensored-hauhaucs-aggressive" = "Qwen 3.6 35B A3B Uncensored Hauhaucs Aggressive"
    "qwen3.8-27b"                                    = "Unsloth Qwen 3.8 27B"
    "qwen3.8-27b-uncensored-hauhaucs-aggressive-mtp" = "Qwen 3.8 27B Uncensored Hauhaucs Aggressive MTP"
    "recursivesi/flint"                              = "RecursiveSI Flint 40B"
    "text-embedding-nomic-embed-text-v1.5"           = "Text Embedding Nomic Embed Text v1.5"
    "unsloth/qwen3-coder-next"                       = "Qwen 3 Coder Next 80B-A3B (Unsloth Q4_K_M)"
}

# 2. Per-model context limits (reasonable limits erroring on higher side <= 100k)
$contextMap = @{
    "text-embedding-nomic-embed-text-v1.5"           = @{ maxInput = 2048;  maxOutput = 512 }
    "qwen3-1.7b"                                     = @{ maxInput = 32768; maxOutput = 4096 }
    "google/gemma-4-e4b"                             = @{ maxInput = 49152; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "ibm/granite-4-h-tiny"                           = @{ maxInput = 49152; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "qwen/qwen3-4b-2507"                             = @{ maxInput = 49152; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-4b"                      = @{ maxInput = 49152; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "glm-4.7-flash"                                  = @{ maxInput = 49152; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni"                    = @{ maxInput = 49152; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "meta/muse-glimmer"                              = @{ maxInput = 49152; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "deepseek/deepseek-r1-0528-qwen3-8b"             = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "google/gemma-4-12b"                             = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "google/gemma-4-12b-qat"                         = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "gemma-4-12b-heretic-abliterated"               = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "nousresearch/hermes-4-70b"                      = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-nano"                         = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-super"                        = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl"                   = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "openai/gpt-oss-20b"                             = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "qwen/qwen3-coder-30b"                           = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"                          = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "qwen/qwen3.5-9b"                                = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b"                           = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "qwen3-coder-30b-a3b-instruct"                   = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "qwen3.5-122b-a10b"                              = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "qwen3.6-35b-a3b"                                = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "qwen3.6-35b-a3b-uncensored-hauhaucs-aggressive" = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "qwen3.8-27b-uncensored-hauhaucs-aggressive-mtp" = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "recursivesi/flint"                              = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "unsloth/qwen3-coder-next"                       = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "gpt-oss-120b"                                   = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "google/gemma-4-26b-a4b"                         = @{ maxInput = 94208; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-qat"                     = @{ maxInput = 94208; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "google/gemma-4-31b"                             = @{ maxInput = 94208; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "google/gemma-4-31b-qat"                         = @{ maxInput = 94208; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "qwen/qwen3.8-27b"                               = @{ maxInput = 94208; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "qwen3.8-27b"                                    = @{ maxInput = 94208; maxOutput = 8192 }
}

# 3. Wake LM-Link service and load dynamic metadata from 'lms ls --json'
Write-Host "Checking LM-Link status..." -ForegroundColor Cyan
$linkOut = lms link status 2>&1 | Out-String
if ($linkOut -match "Waking up") { Start-Sleep -Seconds 3 }

$jsonMeta = @{}
try {
    $lmsJson = lms ls --json | ConvertFrom-Json
    foreach ($m in $lmsJson) {
        if (-not $jsonMeta.ContainsKey($m.modelKey)) {
            $jsonMeta[$m.modelKey] = $m
        }
    }
} catch {}

function Build-ModelEntry($id, $url) {
    $meta = $jsonMeta[$id]
    $displayName = if ($nameMap.ContainsKey($id)) {
        $nameMap[$id]
    } elseif ($meta -and $meta.displayName) {
        $meta.displayName
    } else {
        $id
    }

    $limits = if ($contextMap.ContainsKey($id)) {
        $contextMap[$id]
    } elseif ($meta) {
        if ($meta.type -eq "embedding" -or $meta.maxContextLength -le 4096) {
            @{ maxInput = 2048; maxOutput = 512 }
        } elseif ($meta.maxContextLength -le 40960) {
            @{ maxInput = 32768; maxOutput = 4096 }
        } else {
            @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
        }
    } else {
        @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    }

    return [ordered]@{
        id              = $id
        name            = $displayName
        url             = $url
        toolCalling     = $true
        vision          = $true
        maxInputTokens  = $limits.maxInput
        maxOutputTokens = $limits.maxOutput
    }
}

# 4. Parse LMS authoritative device list
Write-Host "Fetching authoritative device list from 'lms ls'..." -ForegroundColor Cyan
$lmsLines = lms ls
$localIds = @()
$amdHaloIds = @()
$ripperIds = @()
$geforceIds = @()
$otherRemoteIds = @()

foreach ($line in $lmsLines) {
    if ($line -match '^\s*([^\s(]+)(?:\s+\(\d+\s+variant\w*\))?\s+') {
        $id = $matches[1]
        if ($line -match '\s+(Local|amd-halo|ripper|GeForce|DTE-macOS-\S+)\b') {
            $device = $matches[1]
            if ($device -eq 'Local') { $localIds += $id }
            elseif ($device -eq 'amd-halo') { $amdHaloIds += $id }
            elseif ($device -eq 'ripper') { $ripperIds += $id }
            elseif ($device -eq 'GeForce') { $geforceIds += $id }
            else { $otherRemoteIds += $id }
        }
    }
}

$localIds = $localIds | Sort-Object -Unique
$amdHaloIds = $amdHaloIds | Sort-Object -Unique
$ripperIds = $ripperIds | Sort-Object -Unique
$geforceIds = $geforceIds | Sort-Object -Unique
$otherRemoteIds = $otherRemoteIds | Sort-Object -Unique

# 5. Fetch cluster models via loopback for LM-Link and Remote
Write-Host "Fetching cluster models from http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1/models..." -ForegroundColor Cyan
$apiModels = (Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1/models").data | Select-Object -ExpandProperty id
$lmLinkIds = ($apiModels | Sort-Object -Unique)
$remoteIds = ($amdHaloIds + $ripperIds + $geforceIds + $otherRemoteIds | Sort-Object -Unique)

# 6. Construct category objects
$categories = @(
    [ordered]@{
        name    = "Local"
        vendor  = "customendpoint"
        apiType = "chat-completions"
        models  = @($localIds | ForEach-Object { Build-ModelEntry $_ "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1" })
    },
    [ordered]@{
        name    = "LM-Link"
        vendor  = "customendpoint"
        apiType = "chat-completions"
        models  = @($lmLinkIds | ForEach-Object { Build-ModelEntry $_ "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1" })
    },
    [ordered]@{
        name     = "ripper"
        vendor   = "customendpoint"
        apiType  = "chat-completions"
        models   = @($ripperIds | ForEach-Object { Build-ModelEntry $_ "http://ripper:1234/v1" })
    },
    [ordered]@{
        name     = "geforce"
        vendor   = "customendpoint"
        apiType  = "chat-completions"
        models   = @($geforceIds | ForEach-Object { Build-ModelEntry $_ "http://geforce:1234/v1" })
    },
    [ordered]@{
        name     = "LM-Link"
        vendor   = "customendpoint"
        apiType  = "chat-completions"
        models   = @($lmLinkIds | ForEach-Object { Build-ModelEntry $_ "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1" })
    },
    [ordered]@{
        name     = "Remote"
        vendor   = "customendpoint"
        apiType  = "chat-completions"
        models   = @($remoteIds | ForEach-Object { Build-ModelEntry $_ "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1" })
    }
)

$jsonContent = $categories | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 5

# 7. Resolve target paths (base User configuration + active/existing profiles)
$targets = @("$env:APPDATA\Code\User\chatLanguageModels.json")

$activeProfileDir = Get-ChildItem "$env:APPDATA\Code\User\profiles\*\globalStorage" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |
    Sort-Object LastWriteTime -Descending | Select-Object -First 1 | ForEach-Object { $_.Parent }

if ($activeProfileDir) {
    $targets += (Join-Path $activeProfileDir.FullName "chatLanguageModels.json")
}

Get-ChildItem "$env:APPDATA\Code\User\profiles" -Directory -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | ForEach-Object {
    $p = Join-Path $_.FullName "chatLanguageModels.json"
    if (Test-Path $p) { $targets += $p }
}

$targets = $targets | Select-Object -Unique

# 8. Validate & Write
foreach ($target in $targets) {
    if (Test-Path $target) {
        Copy-Item -Path $target -Destination "$target.bak" -Force
        Write-Host "Created backup: $target.bak"
    }
    [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($target, $jsonContent, [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8)
    Write-Host "Successfully updated: $target" -ForegroundColor Green

    $null = Get-Content $target -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
}

# 9. Verify no localhost or 169.254. occurrences
$invalidMatches = Select-String -Path $targets -Pattern 'localhost|169\.254\.'
if ($invalidMatches.Count -gt 0) {
    Write-Warning "Found invalid URLs in output!"
    $invalidMatches | Format-Table LineNumber, Line
} else {
    Write-Host "URL verification passed (0 invalid URLs)." -ForegroundColor Green
}

Write-Host "To apply changes in VS Code, run: code --reload-window" -ForegroundColor Cyan
```

---

## 9. Cross-Platform Python 3 Script (macOS / Linux / Windows)

On macOS (`DTE-macOS-*`), Linux, or Windows with Python 3 installed, run:

```python
#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Automates VS Code chatLanguageModels.json updates across macOS, Linux, and Windows."""
import json
import os
import platform
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import time
import urllib.request
from pathlib import Path

NAME_MAP = {
    "deepseek/deepseek-r1-0528-qwen3-8b": "DeepSeek R1 0528 Qwen3 8B",
    "gemma-4-12b-heretic-abliterated": "Gemma 4 12B Heretic Abliterated",
    "glm-4.7-flash": "GLM 4.7 Flash",
    "google/gemma-4-12b": "Gemma 4 12B",
    "google/gemma-4-12b-qat": "Gemma 4 12B QAT",
    "google/gemma-4-26b-a4b": "Gemma 4 26B A4B",
    "google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-qat": "Gemma 4 26B A4B QAT",
    "google/gemma-4-31b": "Gemma 4 31B",
    "google/gemma-4-31b-qat": "Gemma 4 31B QAT",
    "google/gemma-4-e4b": "Gemma 4 E4B",
    "gpt-oss-120b": "Lemonade GPT OSS 120B (Q4_K_M)",
    "ibm/granite-4-h-tiny": "Granite 4 H Tiny",
    "meta/muse-glimmer": "Meta Muse Glimmer 28B",
    "nousresearch/hermes-4-70b": "Hermes 4 70B",
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-nano": "Nemotron 3 Nano",
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-4b": "Nemotron 3 Nano 4B",
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni": "Nemotron 3 Nano Omni 30B-A3B",
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-super": "Nemotron 3 Super 120B",
    "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl": "Nemotron 3.5 Super VL 120B",
    "openai/gpt-oss-20b": "OpenAI GPT-OSS 20B",
    "qwen/qwen3-4b-2507": "Qwen 3 4B 2507",
    "qwen/qwen3-coder-30b": "Qwen 3 Coder 30B",
    "qwen/qwen3-coder-next": "Qwen 3 Coder Next",
    "qwen/qwen3.5-9b": "Qwen 3.5 9B",
    "qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b": "Qwen 3.6 35B A3B",
    "qwen/qwen3.8-27b": "Qwen 3.8 27B",
    "qwen3-1.7b": "Qwen 3 1.7B",
    "qwen3-coder-30b-a3b-instruct": "Unsloth Qwen 3 Coder 30B A3B Instruct",
    "qwen3.5-122b-a10b": "Qwen 3.5 122B A10B (Unsloth Q4_K_M)",
    "qwen3.6-35b-a3b": "Qwen 3.6 35B A3B (Unsloth Q8_0)",
    "qwen3.6-35b-a3b-uncensored-hauhaucs-aggressive": "Qwen 3.6 35B A3B Uncensored Hauhaucs Aggressive",
    "qwen3.8-27b": "Unsloth Qwen 3.8 27B",
    "qwen3.8-27b-uncensored-hauhaucs-aggressive-mtp": "Qwen 3.8 27B Uncensored Hauhaucs Aggressive MTP",
    "recursivesi/flint": "RecursiveSI Flint 40B",
    "text-embedding-nomic-embed-text-v1.5": "Text Embedding Nomic Embed Text v1.5",
    "unsloth/qwen3-coder-next": "Qwen 3 Coder Next 80B-A3B (Unsloth Q4_K_M)",
}

CONTEXT_MAP = {
    "text-embedding-nomic-embed-text-v1.5": (2048, 512),
    "qwen3-1.7b": (32768, 4096),
    "google/gemma-4-e4b": (49152, 8192),
    "ibm/granite-4-h-tiny": (49152, 8192),
    "qwen/qwen3-4b-2507": (49152, 8192),
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-4b": (49152, 8192),
    "glm-4.7-flash": (49152, 8192),
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni": (49152, 8192),
    "meta/muse-glimmer": (49152, 8192),
    "google/gemma-4-26b-a4b": (94208, 8192),
    "google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-qat": (94208, 8192),
    "google/gemma-4-31b": (94208, 8192),
    "google/gemma-4-31b-qat": (94208, 8192),
    "qwen/qwen3.8-27b": (94208, 8192),
    "qwen3.8-27b": (94208, 8192),
}

def main():
    link = subprocess.run(["lms", "link", "status"], capture_output=True, text=True)
    if "Waking up" in (link.stdout + link.stderr):
        time.sleep(3)

    json_meta = {}
    res_json = subprocess.run(["lms", "ls", "--json"], capture_output=True, text=True)
    if res_json.returncode == 0:
        for item in json.loads(res_json.stdout):
            json_meta.setdefault(item.get("modelKey"), item)

    res_ls = subprocess.run(["lms", "ls"], capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)
    buckets = {"Local": set(), "amd-halo": set(), "ripper": set(), "GeForce": set(), "OtherRemote": set()}
    for line in res_ls.stdout.splitlines():
        m_id = re.match(r"^\s*([^\s(]+)(?:\s+\(\d+\s+variant\w*\))?\s+", line)
        m_dev = re.search(r"\s+(Local|amd-halo|ripper|GeForce|DTE-macOS-\S+)\b", line)
        if m_id and m_dev:
            mid, dev = m_id.group(1), m_dev.group(1)
            buckets[dev if dev in buckets else "OtherRemote"].add(mid)

    with urllib.request.urlopen("http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1/models", timeout=5) as resp:
        api_models = sorted({m["id"] for m in json.loads(resp.read().decode())["data"]})

    def build_entry(mid, url):
        meta = json_meta.get(mid, {})
        name = NAME_MAP.get(mid) or meta.get("displayName") or mid
        if mid in CONTEXT_MAP:
            max_in, max_out = CONTEXT_MAP[mid]
        elif meta.get("type") == "embedding" or meta.get("maxContextLength", 65536) <= 4096:
            max_in, max_out = 2048, 512
        elif meta.get("maxContextLength", 65536) <= 40960:
            max_in, max_out = 32768, 4096
        else:
            max_in, max_out = 65536, 8192
        return {
            "id": mid, "name": name, "url": url,
            "toolCalling": True, "vision": True,
            "maxInputTokens": max_in, "maxOutputTokens": max_out,
        }

    remote_ids = sorted(buckets["amd-halo"] | buckets["ripper"] | buckets["GeForce"] | buckets["OtherRemote"])
    categories = [
        {"name": "Local", "vendor": "customendpoint", "apiType": "chat-completions",
         "models": [build_entry(m, "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1") for m in sorted(buckets["Local"])]},
        {"name": "amd-halo", "vendor": "customendpoint", "apiType": "chat-completions",
         "models": [build_entry(m, "http://amd-halo:1234/v1") for m in sorted(buckets["amd-halo"])]},
        {"name": "ripper", "vendor": "customendpoint", "apiType": "chat-completions",
         "models": [build_entry(m, "http://ripper:1234/v1") for m in sorted(buckets["ripper"])]},
        {"name": "geforce", "vendor": "customendpoint", "apiType": "chat-completions",
         "models": [build_entry(m, "http://geforce:1234/v1") for m in sorted(buckets["GeForce"])]},
        {"name": "LM-Link", "vendor": "customendpoint", "apiType": "chat-completions",
         "models": [build_entry(m, "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1") for m in api_models]},
        {"name": "Remote", "vendor": "customendpoint", "apiType": "chat-completions",
         "models": [build_entry(m, "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1") for m in remote_ids]},
    ]

    sys_name = platform.system()
    if sys_name == "Windows":
        code_user = Path(os.environ["APPDATA"]) / "Code" / "User"
    elif sys_name == "Darwin":
        code_user = Path.home() / "Library" / "Application Support" / "Code" / "User"
    else:
        code_user = Path.home() / ".config" / "Code" / "User"

    targets = {code_user / "chatLanguageModels.json"}
    profiles_dir = code_user / "profiles"
    if profiles_dir.is_dir():
        gs_dirs = sorted(profiles_dir.glob("*/globalStorage"), key=lambda p: p.stat().st_mtime, reverse=True)
        if gs_dirs:
            targets.add(gs_dirs[0].parent / "chatLanguageModels.json")
        for p in profiles_dir.glob("*/chatLanguageModels.json"):
            targets.add(p)

    payload = json.dumps(categories, indent=2)
    for t in sorted(targets):
        if t.exists():
            shutil.copy2(t, f"{t}.bak")
        t.write_text(payload, encoding="utf-8")
        json.loads(t.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        print(f"Updated: {t}")

if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
```
